  {
   "title": "Little words that push ba back",
   "blocks": [
    {
     "type": "p",
     "t": "Sometimes short one-syllable words are added for emphasis: the personal pronouns **ka, ko** and **mo**, and particles such as **na, pa, din, daw, pô, hô, ngâ** and others. They follow the question word (or the predicate) and push **ba** further toward the end of the question."
    },
    {
     "type": "p",
     "t": "Ba actually belongs to the same group as these particles. They are optional, but they add emphasis."
    },
    {
     "type": "table",
     "head": [
      "Particle",
      "Meaning",
      "Example"
     ],
     "rows": [
      [
       "[[na|part]]",
       "*already* or *now*; expresses finality",
       "Aalís na ba silá? *Will they leave already?*"
      ],
      [
       "[[pa|part]]",
       "*still, yet* or *more*",
       "Marumí pa ba siyá? *Is he/she still dirty?*"
      ],
      [
       "[[din|part]] / [[rin|part]]",
       "*too* and *also*. **Din** after a word ending in a consonant, **rin** after a word ending in a vowel",
       "Ikáw din ba? *You too?*  Akó rin ba? *Me too?*"
      ],
      [
       "[[daw|part]] / [[raw|part]]",
       "*they say* or *reportedly*; the speaker got the information from another source. **Daw** after a consonant, **raw** after a vowel",
       "Ikáw daw. *They say it is you.*  Akó raw. *They say it is I.*"
      ],
      [
       "[[ngâ|part]]",
       "*indeed*; also puts emphasis on the word before it",
       ""
      ]
     ],
     "title": "Particles"
    },
