 "recap": [
  "Ba has no translation: it is a spoken question mark. Raise your voice at the end of a yes-or-no question.",
  "Subject first: ba goes after the subject, before ay (Ang babáe ba ay mabaít?). Ba + ay can become ba'y.",
  "Predicate first: ba goes after the predicate (Mabaít ba ang babáe?).",
  "With a question word, ba follows it (Síno ba ang kasáma mo?), and the answer is not yes or no.",
  "Ka, ko, mo and the particles na, pa, din/rin, daw/raw, ngâ push ba further back (Aalís ka na ba?).",
  "After a pseudo verb use bang (Gustó bang kumáin ng batà?), unless a pronoun follows ba (Dápat ba siyáng magsalitâ?)."
 ]
